To solve this, we first find the value of $g(-3)$ by substituting $x = -3$ into $g(x)$:
\begin{align*}
g(-3) &= 3(-3) + 4 \\
&= -9 + 4 \\
&= -5
\end{align*}
Now, we substitute the result into $f(x)$:
\begin{align*}
f(g(-3)) &= f(-5) \\
&= (-5)^2 \\
&= 25
\end{align*}
<u>Answer: </u>
\begin{align*}
f(g(-3)) = 25
\end{align*}

